 106:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** /* Private functions ---------------------------------------------------------*/
 107:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 108:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** /** @defgroup RCC_Exported_Functions RCC Exported Functions
 109:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *  @{
 110:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****   */
 111:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 112:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** /** @defgroup RCC_Exported_Functions_Group1 Initialization and de-initialization functions
 113:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *  @brief    Initialization and Configuration functions
 114:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *
 115:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** @verbatim
 116:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****  ===============================================================================
 117:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****            ##### Initialization and de-initialization functions #####
 118:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****  ===============================================================================
 119:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
 120:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****       This section provides functions allowing to configure the internal/external oscillators
 121:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (HSE, HSI, LSE, LSI, PLL, CSS and MCO) and the System busses clocks (SYSCLK, AHB, APB1
 122:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****        and APB2).
 123:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 124:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..] Internal/external clock and PLL configuration
 125:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) HSI (high-speed internal), 16 MHz factory-trimmed RC used directly or through
 126:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              the PLL as System clock source.
 127:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 128:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) LSI (low-speed internal), 32 KHz low consumption RC used as IWDG and/or RTC
 129:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              clock source.
 130:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 131:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) HSE (high-speed external), 4 to 26 MHz crystal oscillator used directly or
 132:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              through the PLL as System clock source. Can be used also as RTC clock source.
 133:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 134:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) LSE (low-speed external), 32 KHz oscillator used as RTC clock source.
 135:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 136:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) PLL (clocked by HSI or HSE), featuring two different output clocks:
 137:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****            (++) The first output is used to generate the high speed system clock (up to 168 MHz)
 138:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****            (++) The second output is used to generate the clock for the USB OTG FS (48 MHz),
 139:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****                 the random analog generator (<=48 MHz) and the SDIO (<= 48 MHz).
 140:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 141:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) CSS (Clock security system), once enable using the macro __HAL_RCC_CSS_ENABLE()
 142:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              and if a HSE clock failure occurs(HSE used directly or through PLL as System
 143:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              clock source), the System clocks automatically switched to HSI and an interrupt
 144:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              is generated if enabled. The interrupt is linked to the Cortex-M4 NMI
 145:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              (Non-Maskable Interrupt) exception vector.
 146:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 147:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) MCO1 (microcontroller clock output), used to output HSI, LSE, HSE or PLL
 148:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              clock (through a configurable prescaler) on PA8 pin.
 149:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 150:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) MCO2 (microcontroller clock output), used to output HSE, PLL, SYSCLK or PLLI2S
 151:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              clock (through a configurable prescaler) on PC9 pin.
 152:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 153:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..] System, AHB and APB busses clocks configuration
 154:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) Several clock sources can be used to drive the System clock (SYSCLK): HSI,
 155:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              HSE and PLL.
 156:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              The AHB clock (HCLK) is derived from System clock through configurable
 157:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              prescaler and used to clock the CPU, memory and peripherals mapped
 158:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              on AHB bus (DMA, GPIO...). APB1 (PCLK1) and APB2 (PCLK2) clocks are derived
 159:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              from AHB clock through configurable prescalers and used to clock
 160:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              the peripherals mapped on these busses. You can use
 161:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_rcc.c ****              "HAL_RCC_GetSysClockFreq()" function to retrieve the frequencies of these clocks.
